window.ORCL_ANALYSTS = {"generatedAt":"2026-10-30T01:21:10.426Z","asOf":"2026-10-13","windowDays":60,"windowStart":"2026-08-14","libraryNote":{"en":"Reports dated from Aug 14 to Oct 13, 2026 in the owner's research library (Archives folder for August and September, Current folder for October): every report on Oracle was read in full; summaries are FNAM's, figures are the houses'. Two houses (Mizuho, Yorkville Ives) are known only through press copies of their notes and are labeled as such.","es":"Reportes fechados del 14 de agosto al 13 de octubre de 2026 en la biblioteca de investigación de la responsable (carpeta Archives para agosto y septiembre, Current para octubre): cada reporte sobre Oracle se leyó completo; los resúmenes son de FNAM, las cifras son de cada casa. Dos casas (Mizuho, Yorkville Ives) se conocen solo por copias de prensa de sus notas y así se etiquetan."},"priceNote":{"en":"'vs price' compares each target with the latest close in the model; the price the house saw on its report date is shown beside it. Targets are 12-month unless the house says otherwise.","es":"'vs precio' compara cada objetivo con el último cierre del modelo; al lado se muestra el precio que la casa tenía en la fecha de su reporte. Los objetivos son a 12 meses salvo que la casa indique otra cosa."},"houses":[{"id":"db","house":"Deutsche Bank","kind":"equity","analysts":"Brad Zelnick, Bhavin Shah","date":"2026-09-11","title":"Oracle: F1Q - Delivering the Goods","rating":"Buy","rating_class":"buy","target_usd":300,"target_prev_usd":300,"target_history":[{"date":"2025-10-17","usd":375},{"date":"2026-03-08","usd":300}],"price_at_report":152.94,"price_date":"2026-09-10","basis_short_en":"Out-year revenue and operating-income forecasts; FY2030 EPS x P/E discounted at a 12% cost of equity (Aug 7 note)","basis_short_es":"Pronósticos de ingresos y utilidad de operación de años futuros; UPA AF2030 x P/U descontada a un costo de capital de 12% (nota del 7 de agosto)","method_en":"The US$300 target is reiterated on the house's raised out-year forecasts (FY27/FY28 revenue US$90.7 bn / US$129.7 bn; Non-GAAP operating income US$36.3 bn / US$48.9 bn). The August 7 note frames value as FY2030 EPS times a P/E multiple discounted to the present at a 12% cost of equity, and flexes EPS for a funding mix of 0% to 100% equity at US$150 and US$100 per share.","method_es":"El objetivo de US$300 se reitera sobre los pronósticos elevados de años futuros (ingresos AF27/AF28 de US$90.7 mil M / US$129.7 mil M; utilidad de operación No-GAAP de US$36.3 mil M / US$48.9 mil M). La nota del 7 de agosto plantea el valor como la UPA del AF2030 por un múltiplo P/U, descontada al presente a un costo de capital de 12%, y sensibiliza la UPA a una mezcla de financiamiento de 0% a 100% en acciones a US$150 y US$100 por acción.","thesis_en":"Fiscal 1Q beat on both lines and the quarter removed two overhangs: the US$20 bn at-the-market equity program is complete, and the US$30 bn-plus of new AI contracts came through prepayment or bring-your-own-hardware structures that need no additional capital from Oracle. OCI accelerated almost 30 points to +120% in constant currency (about 5 points above the Street) on a record 850 MW delivered and more than 300,000 GPUs; capacity coming up for renewal re-priced at a 20% premium. Gross margin fell 7.7 points to 61.0% as expected, offset by operating expenses down 9%, so the Non-GAAP operating margin still expanded and Non-GAAP EPS of US$1.92 grew 30%. FY27 revenue is now 'at least' US$90 bn and EPS US$8.10; capex of US$90-95 bn gross with net cash capex capped at US$70 bn was reiterated. Watch items: cloud database growth slowed to 26%, SaaS (+10%) and license (-14%) came in below the Street, and free cash flow was -US$5.4 bn on US$28.5 bn of capex. The October 28 analyst meeting is the next catalyst: the OCI buildout, capital-light funding models, the AI Data Platform and the new CFO's long-term targets.","thesis_es":"El 1T fiscal superó en ingresos y utilidad, y el trimestre despejó dos lastres: el programa de colocación de acciones en el mercado por US$20 mil M quedó completo, y los más de US$30 mil M de nuevos contratos de IA llegaron con estructuras de prepago o de hardware aportado por el cliente que no requieren capital adicional de Oracle. OCI aceleró casi 30 puntos a +120% a tipo de cambio constante (unos 5 puntos arriba del consenso) con un récord de 850 MW entregados y más de 300,000 GPUs; la capacidad que venció se renovó con una prima de 20%. El margen bruto cayó 7.7 puntos a 61.0% como se esperaba, compensado por gastos de operación -9%, de modo que el margen operativo No-GAAP aun se expandió y la UPA No-GAAP de US$1.92 creció 30%. Los ingresos del AF27 son ahora de 'al menos' US$90 mil M y la UPA de US$8.10; se reiteró el capex de US$90-95 mil M bruto con un tope de US$70 mil M neto en efectivo. Puntos a vigilar: el crecimiento de la base de datos en la nube bajó a 26%, SaaS (+10%) y licencias (-14%) quedaron debajo del consenso, y el flujo libre fue de -US$5.4 mil M con capex de US$28.5 mil M. La reunión con analistas del 28 de octubre es el siguiente catalizador: la expansión de OCI, los modelos de financiamiento ligeros en capital, la AI Data Platform y los objetivos de largo plazo de la nueva directora financiera.","risks_en":"Key-person risk, a change in the competitive environment, the IT-spending cycle, customer concentration and the ability to ramp cloud-infrastructure capacity.","risks_es":"Riesgo de persona clave, cambios en el entorno competitivo, el ciclo de gasto en TI, concentración de clientes y la capacidad de escalar la infraestructura de nube.","earlier":[],"source":{"basis":"report","title":"Deutsche Bank Research, Oracle: F1Q - Delivering the Goods, 11 September 2026; owner's research library, not republished"}},{"id":"ubs","house":"UBS","kind":"equity","analysts":"Karl Keirstead, Radi Sultan","date":"2026-09-10","title":"Oracle Corporation: AI Bends the Growth Curve Higher","rating":"Buy","rating_class":"buy","target_usd":250,"target_prev_usd":245,"target_history":[{"date":"2026-06-01","usd":285},{"date":"2026-08-05","usd":245},{"date":"2026-09-10","usd":250}],"price_at_report":152.94,"price_date":"2026-09-10","basis_short_en":"19x CY2028E non-GAAP EPS, multiple unchanged","basis_short_es":"19x la UPA No-GAAP estimada de 2028 calendario, múltiplo sin cambio","method_en":"Price target raised to US$250 from US$245 on an unchanged 19x multiple of CY2028E non-GAAP EPS; on CY27 estimates the shares trade at 23x GAAP and 18x non-GAAP EPS, attractive given the growth acceleration and the pending backlog conversion (the report's standing valuation disclosure for the stock describes an FCF-multiple method). Forecast stock return 64.8%.","method_es":"Precio objetivo elevado a US$250 desde US$245 con un múltiplo sin cambio de 19x la UPA No-GAAP estimada de 2028 calendario; con las estimaciones de 2027 calendario la acción cotiza a 23x la UPA GAAP y 18x la No-GAAP, atractivo dada la aceleración del crecimiento y la conversión pendiente de la cartera (la declaración de valuación permanente del reporte describe un método de múltiplo de flujo libre). Rendimiento esperado de la acción: 64.8%.","thesis_en":"The AI-driven acceleration is playing out: revenue growth of 30% against 11% a year earlier, a beat on revenue and EPS, operating expenses down 9% to offset gross-margin pressure, a backlog growing with more customer diversity and 850 MW stood up in the quarter. The guide for infrastructure revenue to keep accelerating through FY27 was better than the stable growth UBS had modeled; capex of US$90-95 bn was reaffirmed with dollar capex expected to peak in FY27 or FY28; the completed US$20 bn equity program and the statement that no further financing is needed this calendar year relieve some credit risk; renewals re-priced 20%-plus and Oracle signaled that US$10 bn of revenue per GW may prove conservative. Negatives: the FY27 revenue guide was only reaffirmed at US$90 bn, the 2Q range is unusually wide, and the 61% gross margin came in below UBS's 62%.","thesis_es":"La aceleración impulsada por la IA se está materializando: crecimiento de ingresos de 30% frente a 11% un año antes, resultados por encima de lo esperado en ingresos y UPA, gastos de operación -9% para compensar la presión en el margen bruto, una cartera que crece con más diversidad de clientes y 850 MW puestos en marcha en el trimestre. La guía de que los ingresos de infraestructura sigan acelerando durante el AF27 fue mejor que el crecimiento estable que UBS modelaba; se reafirmó el capex de US$90-95 mil M con el pico esperado en el AF27 o AF28; el programa de acciones por US$20 mil M completado y la declaración de que no se necesita más financiamiento este año calendario alivian parte del riesgo de crédito; las renovaciones se repreciaron con más de 20% y Oracle señaló que los US$10 mil M de ingresos por GW podrían quedarse cortos. Negativos: la guía de ingresos del AF27 solo se reafirmó en US$90 mil M, el rango del 2T es inusualmente amplio y el margen bruto de 61% quedó debajo del 62% de UBS.","estimates":{"FY2027":{"revenue_usd_bn":90.4,"eps":8.18},"FY2028":{"revenue_usd_bn":130.1,"eps":10.89},"FY2029":{"revenue_usd_bn":176.4,"eps":15.43},"FY2030":{"revenue_usd_bn":209.7,"eps":18.93}},"risks_en":"Downside: execution risk from the sales re-organization and slipped deals, limited traction of the cloud offering and tougher competition; upside: share gains against Workday and SAP (the report's standing risk statement).","risks_es":"A la baja: riesgo de ejecución por la reorganización comercial y acuerdos diferidos, tracción limitada de la oferta de nube y mayor competencia; al alza: ganancias de participación frente a Workday y SAP (declaración de riesgos permanente del reporte).","source":{"basis":"report","title":"UBS Global Research, Oracle Corporation: AI Bends the Growth Curve Higher, 10 September 2026; owner's research library, not republished"}},{"id":"gs","house":"Goldman Sachs","kind":"equity","analysts":"Gabriela Borges (Oracle coverage); Eric Sheridan, James Schneider and team (thematic)","date":"2026-09-24","title":"Americas Technology: Sizing the AI Economy Needed to Justify ROIC on Hyperscaler AI Capex","rating":"Buy","rating_class":"buy","target_usd":240,"target_prev_usd":null,"price_at_report":null,"price_date":null,"basis_short_en":"15x 2030E adjusted net income, discounted back to the second-next-twelve-months window","basis_short_es":"15x la utilidad neta ajustada estimada de 2030, descontada a la ventana de los segundos doce meses siguientes","method_en":"The US$240 12-month price target is 15x Oracle's 2030E adjusted net income, discounted back to the second-next-twelve-months window (quarters 5 to 8). The company note of September 14 ('1QFY: Backlog conversion begins to emerge; FY28 capital intensity still in focus') is listed in the house's research recap but is not in the library; the rating and target come from the thematic report.","method_es":"El precio objetivo a 12 meses de US$240 es 15x la utilidad neta ajustada estimada de Oracle para 2030, descontada a la ventana de los segundos doce meses siguientes (trimestres 5 a 8). La nota de la empresa del 14 de septiembre ('1QFY: Backlog conversion begins to emerge; FY28 capital intensity still in focus') aparece en el resumen de investigación de la casa pero no está en la biblioteca; la recomendación y el objetivo provienen del reporte temático.","thesis_en":"In Goldman's hyperscaler ROIC framework the six large US cloud builders (Alphabet, Amazon, Microsoft, Meta, Oracle and SpaceX) need about US$1.42 tn of cumulative AI revenue in 2028-30, roughly US$11.6 bn per GW per year, to earn a 15% return on their 2026-27 compute investment. For Oracle the framework sets about US$165 bn of upfront 2026-27 capex against roughly US$44.6 bn of annual revenue at a 35% EBIT margin to clear that hurdle, with servers paying back in about three years against a five- to six-year life and shells lasting 30 years; Oracle itself guides to steady-state project ROIC in the high 20s, with upside from longer GPU lives and bring-your-own-hardware, which lowers its upfront capex. The debate, in the house's words, is shifting from how big spending can get to what revenue is needed to justify it.","thesis_es":"En el marco de ROIC de hiperescaladores de Goldman, los seis grandes constructores de nube de EE. UU. (Alphabet, Amazon, Microsoft, Meta, Oracle y SpaceX) necesitan unos US$1.42 billones de ingresos acumulados de IA en 2028-30, alrededor de US$11.6 mil M por GW al año, para obtener un retorno de 15% sobre su inversión en cómputo de 2026-27. Para Oracle el marco contrapone unos US$165 mil M de capex inicial de 2026-27 con cerca de US$44.6 mil M de ingresos anuales a un margen EBIT de 35% para librar esa valla, con servidores que se recuperan en unos tres años frente a una vida de cinco a seis años y naves que duran 30; Oracle guía un ROIC de proyecto en estado estable en los altos 20, con potencial adicional por vidas de GPU más largas y por el hardware aportado por el cliente, que reduce su capex inicial. El debate, en palabras de la casa, pasa de cuánto puede crecer el gasto a qué ingresos se necesitan para justificarlo.","risks_en":"Customer concentration, timing and execution of the data-center buildouts, and intense capex.","risks_es":"Concentración de clientes, calendario y ejecución de la construcción de centros de datos, y capex intenso.","source":{"basis":"report","title":"Goldman Sachs Global Investment Research, Americas Technology: Sizing the AI Economy Needed to Justify ROIC on Hyperscaler AI Capex, 24 September 2026 (Oracle rating and target in its disclosures); owner's research library, not republished"}},{"id":"bofa","house":"BofA Securities","kind":"equity","analysts":"Tal Liani","date":"2026-09-08","title":"Trading Catalysts: CPI and the path for Fed hikes; long-end buyback; and Oracle earnings (1Q27 preview)","rating":"Buy","rating_class":"buy","target_usd":240,"target_prev_usd":null,"price_at_report":158.78,"price_date":"2026-09-04","basis_short_en":"26.5x CY2027E P/E, a premium to large-cap software and cloud data centers at 19x","basis_short_es":"26.5x el P/U estimado de 2027 calendario, prima frente al software de gran capitalización y los centros de datos en la nube a 19x","method_en":"Price objective of US$240 = 26.5x CY2027E P/E, a premium to the large-cap software and cloud data-center group trading at 19x that the house considers warranted by accelerating growth and the mounting backlog. This is the pre-results preview; the post-results update is not in the library.","method_es":"Precio objetivo de US$240 = 26.5x el P/U estimado de 2027 calendario, una prima frente al grupo de software de gran capitalización y centros de datos en la nube que cotiza a 19x, que la casa considera justificada por la aceleración del crecimiento y la cartera creciente. Es la nota previa a los resultados; la actualización posterior no está en la biblioteca.","thesis_en":"Attractive risk/reward into the 1Q27 print after a 25% fall since the 4Q26 results, driven by worries over data-center profitability as component costs rise and credit spreads widen: the Street already captures the difficult balance-sheet picture but not the revenue acceleration that follows the data-center milestones. Three things to watch: capacity deployment and the pace of RPO conversion into revenue, capex and funding requirements, and trends in the core software business.","thesis_es":"Relación riesgo/rendimiento atractiva de cara al reporte del 1T27 tras una caída de 25% desde los resultados del 4T26, por el temor a la rentabilidad de los centros de datos con costos de componentes al alza y diferenciales de crédito más amplios: el consenso ya recoge la difícil posición del balance pero no la aceleración de ingresos que sigue a los hitos de los centros de datos. Tres cosas a vigilar: el despliegue de capacidad y el ritmo de conversión del RPO en ingresos, el capex y las necesidades de financiamiento, y las tendencias del negocio central de software.","risks_en":"Delays in data-center buildouts, a downturn in enterprise software spending, currency headwinds, and software terminal-value pressure from innovative AI labs.","risks_es":"Retrasos en la construcción de centros de datos, una caída del gasto empresarial en software, vientos en contra cambiarios y presión sobre el valor terminal del software por laboratorios de IA innovadores.","source":{"basis":"report","title":"BofA Global Research, Trading Catalysts (Equity and Quant Strategy, with the Oracle 1Q27 preview and price-objective basis), 8 September 2026; owner's research library, not republished"},"label_en":"Pre-results preview: written Sep 8, before the Sep 10 results; the target and its basis predate 1Q27","label_es":"Previa a resultados: escrita el 8 sep, antes de los resultados del 10 sep; el objetivo y su base son anteriores al 1T27"},{"id":"bernstein","house":"Bernstein","kind":"equity","analysts":"Mark L. Moerdler (Oracle coverage), Richard Nguyen, Firoz Valliji, Derric Marcon","date":"2026-09-24","title":"Global Software: The next ERP supercycle (8 Sep) and Data Centers: The impact of Oracle's force majeure on Oracle, Bloom Energy and the data center industry (24 Sep)","rating":"Outperform","rating_class":"buy","target_usd":325,"target_prev_usd":325,"price_at_report":139.54,"price_date":"2026-09-24","basis_short_en":"24.5x adjusted forward P/E on 12-month EPS one year out (US$15.22) plus net cash per share (-US$47.6)","basis_short_es":"24.5x el P/U ajustado adelantado sobre la UPA a 12 meses de dentro de un año (US$15.22) más efectivo neto por acción (-US$47.6)","method_en":"Shares are valued on the house's estimate of 12-month adjusted EPS one year out (US$15.22) at an adjusted forward P/E of 24.5x, adding back net cash per share of -US$47.6, for a US$325 target; ratings and targets reiterated in this sector primer.","method_es":"La acción se valúa con la estimación de la casa de la UPA ajustada a 12 meses de dentro de un año (US$15.22) a un P/U ajustado adelantado de 24.5x, sumando el efectivo neto por acción de -US$47.6, para un objetivo de US$325; recomendaciones y objetivos reiterados en este reporte sectorial.","thesis_en":"ERP is moving from a system of record to a system of execution, a once-in-a-generation platform reset in which the winner controls enterprise work, not just enterprise data. On Bernstein's scorecard Oracle ranks first today thanks to the tight integration of applications, database, cloud infrastructure and ERP, one of the clearest closed-loop execution stories in enterprise software; the trade-off is that its advantage is strongest inside Oracle-centric estates and may count for less in heterogeneous ones. SAP and Microsoft offer the greater strategic upside over the next three years; the bigger risk for all three is that AI-native vendors or neutral orchestration platforms capture the execution layer.","thesis_es":"El ERP pasa de ser un sistema de registro a un sistema de ejecución, un reinicio de plataforma que ocurre una vez por generación y en el que gana quien controla el trabajo de la empresa, no solo sus datos. En la tabla de puntuación de Bernstein, Oracle ocupa hoy el primer lugar gracias a la integración estrecha de aplicaciones, base de datos, infraestructura de nube y ERP, una de las historias de ejecución de ciclo cerrado más claras del software empresarial; la contrapartida es que su ventaja es mayor dentro de entornos centrados en Oracle y puede pesar menos en entornos heterogéneos. SAP y Microsoft ofrecen el mayor potencial estratégico en los próximos tres años; el mayor riesgo para los tres es que proveedores nativos de IA o plataformas neutrales de orquestación capturen la capa de ejecución.","risks_en":"Customer concentration; an AI winter in which generative AI fails globally; database share loss to cloud and alternative databases; slower adoption of SaaS ERP; cybersecurity concerns that reduce cloud demand; weaker demand for the Autonomous and multicloud databases; OCI growth problems, especially at sovereign clouds.","risks_es":"Concentración de clientes; un invierno de la IA en el que la IA generativa fracase globalmente; pérdida de participación de la base de datos frente a bases en la nube y alternativas; adopción más lenta del ERP en SaaS; preocupaciones de ciberseguridad que reduzcan la demanda de nube; menor demanda de las bases de datos Autonomous y multinube; problemas de crecimiento de OCI, sobre todo en nubes soberanas.","source":{"basis":"report","title":"Bernstein, Global Software: The next ERP supercycle, 8 September 2026 (Oracle valuation and risks in its disclosures), and Data Centers: The impact of Oracle's force majeure, 24 September 2026; owner's research library, not republished"},"earlier":[{"date":"2026-09-24","title":"Data Centers: The impact of Oracle's force majeure on Oracle, Bloom Energy and the broader data center industry","rating":"Outperform","target_usd":325,"price_at_report":139.54,"note_en":"The ~4% fall on the Project Jupiter force majeure notice is called an overreaction: the campus was not expected to serve customers before late CY2028 (four buildings of about 225 MW each in Bernstein's estimate), management said neither site affects FY2027 guidance, hyperscalers contract more shell capacity than they need, and the notice gives Oracle options to delay payments to the builder or walk away if the CY2028 go-live is missed. The Bloom Energy fuel-cell contract (up to ~2.5 GW at the site) is seen as intact. Thesis and US$325 target unchanged.","note_es":"La caída de ~4% por el aviso de fuerza mayor en el Proyecto Júpiter se califica de sobrerreacción: el campus no atendería clientes antes de fines de 2028 (cuatro edificios de unos 225 MW cada uno, estimación de Bernstein), la administración dijo que ningún sitio afecta la guía del AF2027, los hiperescaladores contratan más capacidad de la que necesitan y el aviso da a Oracle la opción de retrasar pagos al constructor o retirarse si no se cumple la puesta en marcha de 2028. El contrato de celdas de combustible con Bloom Energy (hasta ~2.5 GW en el sitio) se ve intacto. Tesis y objetivo de US$325 sin cambio."}]},{"id":"bnp","house":"BNP Paribas Exane","kind":"equity","analysts":"Ben Castillo-Bernaus, Ines Mao, Thomas Poutrieux","date":"2026-09-16","title":"Software / IT Services: SaaS Smash - is the SaaSpocalypse over or just pausing","rating":"Outperform","rating_class":"buy","target_usd":null,"target_prev_usd":null,"price_at_report":150,"price_date":"2026-09-15","basis_short_en":"Target not stated in the report on file (sector report; Oracle appears in the ratings and comps tables)","basis_short_es":"Objetivo no indicado en el reporte disponible (reporte sectorial; Oracle aparece en las tablas de recomendaciones y comparables)","method_en":"A European sector report: Oracle carries the Outperform rating in the ratings map and the comps table (price US$150; EV/sales 6.8x, 5.1x and 3.6x and P/E 23x, 19x and 12x for CY26 to CY28) but the report states no target price for it.","method_es":"Reporte sectorial europeo: Oracle lleva la recomendación Outperform en el mapa de recomendaciones y en la tabla de comparables (precio US$150; VE/ventas de 6.8x, 5.1x y 3.6x y P/U de 23x, 19x y 12x para 2026 a 2028 calendario), pero el reporte no indica un precio objetivo.","thesis_en":"The first-quarter software de-rating (more than 50%, with implied terminal values written off to zero) is reversing for vendors that can show AI products at billion-dollar run rates. The market has voted infrastructure and cybersecurity software the proven AI winners; ERP is emerging as a winning category helped by SAP, Sage and Oracle, while CRM and HCM sit at the fork between winner and loser paths and vertical software has yet to go through its 'peak fear' phase.","thesis_es":"La desvalorización del software del primer trimestre (más de 50%, con valores terminales implícitos reducidos a cero) se revierte para los proveedores que muestran productos de IA con ventas anualizadas de miles de millones de dólares. El mercado ha votado al software de infraestructura y de ciberseguridad como ganadores probados de la IA; el ERP emerge como categoría ganadora con ayuda de SAP, Sage y Oracle, mientras CRM y HCM están en la bifurcación entre ganadores y perdedores y el software vertical aún no pasa por su fase de 'miedo máximo'.","risks_en":"Not stated for Oracle in the report on file.","risks_es":"No se indican para Oracle en el reporte disponible.","source":{"basis":"report","title":"BNP Paribas Exane, SaaS Smash: is the SaaSpocalypse over or just pausing (sector report), 16 September 2026; owner's research library, not republished"}},{"id":"barclays","house":"Barclays (credit research)","kind":"credit","analysts":"Andrew Keches, Remy Neuhaus","date":"2026-09-24","title":"ORCL F1Q27 Results: Momentum Builds as ATM Completed (10 Sep) and Quick Take: Force Majeure Declared in New Mexico (24 Sep)","rating":"Overweight (bonds)","rating_class":"credit","target_usd":null,"target_prev_usd":null,"price_at_report":null,"price_date":null,"basis_short_en":"Credit relative value, no equity target: buy the 6.70% 2056s; leverage 3.9x gross and 3.1x net debt to EBITDAR (house estimates)","basis_short_es":"Valor relativo de crédito, sin objetivo accionario: comprar los bonos 6.70% 2056; apalancamiento de 3.9x bruto y 3.1x neto deuda/EBITDAR (estimaciones de la casa)","method_en":"A bond recommendation, not an equity target: Overweight on Oracle's credit with the 6.70% 2056s as the preferred expression (the long end, with room for another 5-10 bp of tightening and some curve flattening). Spreads were about 10 bp tighter after the results, 40 bp off the July wides and still 30 bp wider than after the June results; Barclays estimates gross and net leverage fell to 3.9x and 3.1x debt to EBITDAR from 4.2x and 3.4x on EBITDAR growth, a higher cash balance and US$4.2 bn of debt repaid. The aggregate short base in the bonds exceeds US$5 bn and 5-year CDS remains a hedge for OpenAI and ecosystem exposure, so a larger rally may wait for the October investor day.","method_es":"Una recomendación de bonos, no un objetivo accionario: Overweight en el crédito de Oracle con los bonos 6.70% 2056 como expresión preferida (el extremo largo, con margen para otros 5-10 pb de compresión y cierto aplanamiento de la curva). Los diferenciales se comprimieron unos 10 pb tras los resultados, 40 pb menos que los máximos de julio y aún 30 pb más amplios que tras los resultados de junio; Barclays estima que el apalancamiento bruto y neto bajó a 3.9x y 3.1x deuda/EBITDAR desde 4.2x y 3.4x por el crecimiento del EBITDAR, mayor efectivo y US$4.2 mil M de deuda pagada. La posición corta agregada en los bonos supera US$5 mil M y el CDS a 5 años sigue siendo cobertura de la exposición a OpenAI y su ecosistema, por lo que un repunte mayor puede esperar al día del inversionista de octubre.","thesis_en":"Three consecutive credit-positive quarters: RPO rose US$26 bn to US$664 bn without incremental funding because the new contracts are structured with prepayments and bring-your-own-hardware (OpenAI now at most about 45% of the backlog), the US$20 bn equity program was fully executed, record operating cash flow of US$23.1 bn covered net cash capex of US$18 bn after US$11.4 bn of customer prepayments, and management reiterated FY27 capex of US$90-95 bn gross and no more than US$70 bn net. The less comfortable part is the timeline of the data-center projects, New Mexico above all: the force majeure notice of September 24 is credit-neutral in Barclays' view (lease costs de minimis, about US$30 bn of hardware capex and the related revenue delayed as already expected, FY27 unaffected, FY28 capex phasing possibly changed, no read-across to the Saline, Michigan site, no sign Oracle is walking away). The October investor day is the catalyst for the phasing of capex and free cash flow.","thesis_es":"Tres trimestres consecutivos positivos para el crédito: el RPO subió US$26 mil M a US$664 mil M sin financiamiento incremental porque los contratos nuevos se estructuran con prepagos y hardware aportado por el cliente (OpenAI es ahora a lo sumo 45% de la cartera), el programa de acciones de US$20 mil M se ejecutó por completo, un flujo operativo récord de US$23.1 mil M cubrió un capex neto en efectivo de US$18 mil M tras US$11.4 mil M de prepagos de clientes, y la administración reiteró el capex del AF27 de US$90-95 mil M bruto y no más de US$70 mil M neto. La parte menos cómoda es el calendario de los proyectos de centros de datos, Nuevo México sobre todo: el aviso de fuerza mayor del 24 de septiembre es neutral para el crédito según Barclays (costos de arrendamiento mínimos, unos US$30 mil M de capex de hardware y los ingresos asociados diferidos como ya se esperaba, AF27 sin afectación, posible cambio en el calendario del capex del AF28, sin lectura cruzada al sitio de Saline, Michigan, sin señal de que Oracle abandone el proyecto). El día del inversionista de octubre es el catalizador para el calendario del capex y del flujo libre.","risks_en":"The 'show me' part of the story is the delivery schedule of the campuses that have faced setbacks (New Mexico, Jupiter); a more diversified 2027 funding mix (equity, convertibles, other currencies, chip financing) would be the positive surprise.","risks_es":"La parte de 'demuéstramelo' de la historia es el calendario de entrega de los campus que han sufrido contratiempos (Nuevo México, Jupiter); una mezcla de financiamiento 2027 más diversificada (acciones, convertibles, otras monedas, financiamiento de chips) sería la sorpresa positiva.","source":{"basis":"report","title":"Barclays FICC Research (credit), ORCL F1Q27 Results: Momentum Builds as ATM Completed, 10 September 2026, and Oracle (ORCL): Quick Take - Force Majeure Declared in New Mexico, 24 September 2026; owner's research library, not republished"}},{"id":"ms","house":"Morgan Stanley (credit strategy and accounting research)","kind":"credit","analysts":"Ellie Dann and team (credit strategy); Todd Castagno, Kate Konetzke (valuation, accounting and tax)","date":"2026-10-01","title":"The State of AI Financing: A Pause, Not a Pullback (1 Oct) and AI: Funding the Buildout Beyond the Balance Sheet (25 Aug)","rating":null,"rating_class":null,"target_usd":null,"target_prev_usd":null,"price_at_report":null,"price_date":null,"basis_short_en":"No equity rating or target in the notes on file (credit and accounting research)","basis_short_es":"Sin recomendación ni objetivo accionario en las notas disponibles (investigación de crédito y contabilidad)","method_en":"Neither note carries an equity rating or target: the October 1 piece is credit strategy (Oracle is one of the two single names, with Nvidia, at the center of the house's AI-financing discussions) and the August 25 piece is accounting research on how the buildout is funded beyond operating cash flow.","method_es":"Ninguna de las dos notas trae recomendación ni objetivo accionario: la del 1 de octubre es estrategia de crédito (Oracle es uno de los dos nombres, con Nvidia, en el centro de las discusiones de la casa sobre el financiamiento de la IA) y la del 25 de agosto es investigación contable sobre cómo se financia la expansión más allá del flujo operativo.","thesis_en":"Funding update: the US$20 bn equity program is complete; the house forecasts sizable bond issuance in early calendar 2027 and 2028; customer prepayments have become a meaningful funding source with limited disclosure and a rollover sensitivity; future equity needs depend on the success of prepayments and on cost inflation; lease disclosures imply about 1 GW of shell leases signed in the quarter, and about US$65 bn of short-dated bank and private-credit construction loans fund shells to be leased by Oracle, outside the public bond market. The force majeure notice on Project Jupiter intensified scrutiny of lease documentation (the house prefers stabilized colocation paper over hyperscaler data-center securitisations). The August accounting note counts Oracle's uncommenced leases at US$261 bn at the time, US$18.2 bn of assets acquired under operating leases in FY2026 and US$4.6 bn of customer prepayments used to fund capex, which accrete interest at the incremental borrowing rate until the revenue is recognized: capex is understated and free cash flow overstated to the extent operating leases obtain the construction financing.","thesis_es":"Actualización de financiamiento: el programa de acciones de US$20 mil M está completo; la casa prevé emisiones de bonos considerables a principios de 2027 y en 2028 calendario; los prepagos de clientes se han vuelto una fuente de financiamiento significativa con divulgación limitada y sensibilidad a su renovación; las necesidades futuras de capital dependen del éxito de los prepagos y de la inflación de costos; las revelaciones de arrendamientos implican cerca de 1 GW de naves arrendadas firmadas en el trimestre, y unos US$65 mil M de préstamos de construcción de corto plazo de bancos y crédito privado financian naves que Oracle arrendará, fuera del mercado público de bonos. El aviso de fuerza mayor en el Proyecto Jupiter intensificó el escrutinio de la documentación de los arrendamientos (la casa prefiere el papel de colocación estabilizado sobre las bursatilizaciones de centros de datos de hiperescaladores). La nota contable de agosto contabiliza los arrendamientos no iniciados de Oracle en US$261 mil M en ese momento, US$18.2 mil M de activos adquiridos bajo arrendamiento operativo en el AF2026 y US$4.6 mil M de prepagos de clientes usados para financiar capex, que devengan interés a la tasa incremental de endeudamiento hasta que se reconoce el ingreso: el capex está subestimado y el flujo libre sobreestimado en la medida en que los arrendamientos operativos obtienen el financiamiento de la construcción.","risks_en":"Not applicable: the notes rate neither the shares nor the bonds; they frame the funding, disclosure and documentation questions for the October analyst day.","risks_es":"No aplica: las notas no califican ni la acción ni los bonos; plantean las preguntas de financiamiento, divulgación y documentación para el día del analista de octubre.","source":{"basis":"report","title":"Morgan Stanley Research, The State of AI Financing: A Pause, Not a Pullback, 1 October 2026, and AI: Funding the Buildout Beyond the Balance Sheet, 25 August 2026; owner's research library, not republished"}},{"id":"ms-credit","house":"Morgan Stanley (credit research)","kind":"credit","analysts":"Lindsay A. Tyler, Benjamin Guerrero","date":"2026-09-11","title":"ORCL Credit: New Bookings, Old Bills – FY1Q27 Quick Takes","rating":"Cautious (sell the 2035 and 2055 notes, long 5-year CDS)","rating_class":"credit","target_usd":null,"target_prev_usd":null,"price_at_report":null,"price_date":null,"thesis_en":"1Q27 gives both sides of the debate data points but does not change the cautious view: the US$20 bn ATM is complete and new RPO is increasingly prepay-funded (improving near-term liquidity, with a rollover-like sensitivity if new inflows fund the legacy backlog), while capital intensity, parent funding needs and leverage stay elevated. Through FY2028-end the house still models about US$45 bn of bond funding even with meaningful prepayments, with gross adjusted leverage above Moody's downgrade threshold (above 3.5x through FY2028, pressure into FY2029–30). It would sell into post-print strength ahead of the Investor Day.","thesis_es":"El 1T27 da datos a ambos lados del debate pero no cambia la visión cautelosa: el ATM de US$20 mil M está completo y el nuevo RPO se financia cada vez más con prepagos (mejora la liquidez de corto plazo, con una sensibilidad tipo refinanciamiento si las entradas nuevas financian el backlog anterior), mientras la intensidad de capital, las necesidades de fondeo de la matriz y el apalancamiento siguen elevados. Hasta el cierre del AF2028 la casa aún modela unos US$45 mil M de emisión de bonos incluso con prepagos significativos, con apalancamiento bruto ajustado por encima del umbral de baja de Moody's (más de 3.5x hasta el AF2028, presión hacia 2029–30). Vendería en la fortaleza posterior al reporte antes del Investor Day.","method_en":"Credit view, not an equity target: spread targets of about 200 bp for the 2035 notes and about 250 bp for the 2055 notes (the 2036/2056 notes 10 bp wider), still implying modest widening; about 200 bp or slightly wider as a reasonable 5-year CDS level. Sources and uses FY1Q27–FY2028: gross capex, dividends and maturities against operating cash flow with prepayments, the elevated quarter-end cash and hypothetical bond deals in 1H CY2027 and FY2028.","method_es":"Visión de crédito, no un objetivo de acción: diferenciales objetivo de unos 200 pb para los bonos 2035 y unos 250 pb para los 2055 (los 2036/2056, 10 pb más amplios), que aún implican una ampliación moderada; unos 200 pb o algo más como nivel razonable del CDS a 5 años. Fuentes y usos 1T27–AF2028: capex bruto, dividendos y vencimientos frente al flujo operativo con prepagos, el efectivo elevado al cierre del trimestre y emisiones hipotéticas en el 1S de 2027 y el AF2028.","basis_short_en":"Spread targets ~200 bp (2035s), ~250 bp (2055s); 5-year CDS ~200 bp or wider","basis_short_es":"Diferenciales objetivo ~200 pb (2035), ~250 pb (2055); CDS 5 años ~200 pb o más","risks_en":"Constructive updates on RPO, growth and financing clarity; term loans not serving a significant funding role; CDS technicals (basis selling, construction-loan hedge unwinds, profit taking by outright shorts); an issuance cadence different from the house's assumptions; more visibility on long-term monetization and deleveraging beyond FY2028.","risks_es":"Noticias constructivas sobre RPO, crecimiento y claridad del financiamiento; préstamos a plazo sin un papel relevante de fondeo; factores técnicos del CDS (venta de base, deshacer coberturas de préstamos de construcción, toma de utilidades de cortos); un ritmo de emisión distinto al supuesto por la casa; más visibilidad sobre la monetización y el desapalancamiento de largo plazo más allá del AF2028.","source":{"basis":"report","title":"Morgan Stanley Credit Research (TMT, North America), ORCL Credit: New Bookings, Old Bills – FY1Q27 Quick Takes, 11 September 2026; owner's research library, not republished"}}],"reported":[{"id":"citi","house":"Citi","analysts":"Tyler Radke","date":"2026-08-26","rating":"Buy","rating_class":"buy","target_usd":330,"basis_short_en":"Not reported","basis_short_es":"No reportado","note_en":"Added to Citi's upside 90-day catalyst watch on sustainable earnings growth and ramping AI-infrastructure demand.","note_es":"Incorporada a la lista de vigilancia de catalizadores al alza a 90 días de Citi por el crecimiento sostenible de utilidades y la creciente demanda de infraestructura de IA.","source":{"basis":"streetaccount","title":"FactSet StreetAccount, Oracle added to upside 90-Day Catalyst Watch at Citi, 26 August 2026"}},{"id":"keybanc","house":"KeyBanc","analysts":"Jackson Ader","date":"2026-09-24","rating":"Overweight","rating_class":"buy","target_usd":300,"basis_short_en":"About 27x CY2028 EPS","basis_short_es":"Unas 27x la UPA de 2028 calendario","note_en":"After the results: 120% IaaS growth and 850 MW of new capacity allay fears that project delays would slow near-term revenue recognition; US$26 bn of RPO growth on US$30 bn of new AI bookings from new customers and campuses. After the force majeure notice: a move to avoid paying rent until the site is operational, highlighting the risk of third-party leases whose payment schedules do not match construction timelines and Oracle's weaker cash position than the larger hyperscalers; target unchanged.","note_es":"Tras los resultados: el crecimiento de 120% en IaaS y los 850 MW de capacidad nueva disipan el temor de que los retrasos de proyectos frenen el reconocimiento de ingresos en el corto plazo; US$26 mil M de crecimiento del RPO con US$30 mil M de nuevas contrataciones de IA de clientes y campus nuevos. Tras el aviso de fuerza mayor: una medida para no pagar renta hasta que el sitio opere, que resalta el riesgo de los arrendamientos con terceros cuyos calendarios de pago no coinciden con los de construcción y la posición de efectivo más débil de Oracle frente a los grandes hiperescaladores; objetivo sin cambio.","source":{"basis":"streetaccount","title":"FactSet StreetAccount, Street Takeaways: Oracle Q1 Earnings, 11 September 2026, and Street Takeaways: Oracle sends force majeure notice on Project Jupiter, 24 September 2026"}},{"id":"wells","house":"Wells Fargo Securities","analysts":"Michael Turrin","date":"2026-09-11","rating":"Overweight","rating_class":"buy","target_usd":280,"basis_short_en":"About 22.5x NTM EPS","basis_short_es":"Unas 22.5x la UPA de los siguientes doce meses","note_en":"The report showed Oracle can grow RPO without additional cash outflows and reach its FY targets without a drastic guidance raise; 850 MW is impressive for one quarter but slightly short of the 'close to 1 GW' target; capex still peaks in FY28 and falls in FY29 as the current backlog is funded, with choppy spending through the year on GPU delivery and payment timing.","note_es":"El reporte mostró que Oracle puede hacer crecer el RPO sin salidas adicionales de efectivo y alcanzar sus objetivos del año fiscal sin subir drásticamente la guía; 850 MW es impresionante para un trimestre pero algo corto frente al objetivo de 'cerca de 1 GW'; el capex aún toca su máximo en el AF28 y baja en el AF29 conforme se financia la cartera actual, con gasto irregular durante el año según la entrega y el pago de las GPU.","source":{"basis":"streetaccount","title":"FactSet StreetAccount, Street Takeaways: Oracle Q1 Earnings, 11 September 2026"}},{"id":"piper","house":"Piper Sandler","analysts":"Billy Fitzsimmons","date":"2026-09-11","rating":"Overweight","rating_class":"buy","target_usd":225,"basis_short_en":"Not reported","basis_short_es":"No reportado","note_en":"A solid print that addressed several bear concerns: the capex guide was held against fears of an increase, the full US$20 bn equity financing is done, renewed GPUs resold at a 20% premium prove higher revenue per MW on older hardware, and the FY27 guidance does not rely on the delayed New Mexico and Wisconsin sites; the analyst day is a positive catalyst.","note_es":"Un reporte sólido que atendió varias preocupaciones bajistas: la guía de capex se mantuvo pese al temor a un aumento, el financiamiento accionario completo de US$20 mil M ya se hizo, las GPU renovadas se revendieron con una prima de 20% que prueba mayores ingresos por MW con hardware más antiguo, y la guía del AF27 no depende de los sitios retrasados de Nuevo México y Wisconsin; el día del analista es un catalizador positivo.","source":{"basis":"streetaccount","title":"FactSet StreetAccount, Street Takeaways: Oracle Q1 Earnings, 11 September 2026"}},{"id":"bmo","house":"BMO Capital Markets","analysts":"Keith Bachman","date":"2026-09-11","rating":"Outperform","rating_class":"buy","target_usd":195,"target_prev_usd":220,"basis_short_en":"Not reported","basis_short_es":"No reportado","note_en":"Solid overall but mixed: operating cash flow and operating margins were positive and RPO growth reasonable; gross margins matched the house's estimate but the sequential contraction may concern some, and SaaS growth disappointed slightly. Still bullish; target lowered to US$195 from US$220.","note_es":"Sólido en conjunto pero mixto: el flujo operativo y los márgenes operativos fueron positivos y el crecimiento del RPO razonable; los márgenes brutos coincidieron con la estimación de la casa pero la contracción secuencial puede preocupar a algunos, y el crecimiento de SaaS decepcionó ligeramente. Sigue alcista; objetivo reducido a US$195 desde US$220.","source":{"basis":"streetaccount","title":"FactSet StreetAccount, Street Takeaways: Oracle Q1 Earnings, 11 September 2026"}},{"id":"rbc","house":"RBC Capital Markets","analysts":"Rishi Jaluria","date":"2026-09-24","rating":"Sector Perform","rating_class":"hold","target_usd":165,"target_prev_usd":190,"basis_short_en":"About 17x CY2027 EPS, a target multiple above current levels and in line with peers","basis_short_es":"Unas 17x la UPA de 2027 calendario, múltiplo objetivo por encima del actual y en línea con los pares","note_en":"After the results: a better print with revenue, cloud revenue and EPS above the Street and RPO growth without additional capital, but the house stays watchful on tighter margins and heavy infrastructure investment; target cut to US$165 from US$190. After the force majeure notice: legal cover rather than a cancellation, but every delay threatens revenue recognition and slows RPO conversion, and OpenAI's shift to bilateral capacity leases adds financing uncertainty to the Stargate structure; a wait-and-see stance.","note_es":"Tras los resultados: un mejor reporte con ingresos, ingresos de nube y UPA por encima del consenso y crecimiento del RPO sin capital adicional, pero la casa sigue atenta a márgenes más estrechos y a la fuerte inversión en infraestructura; objetivo recortado a US$165 desde US$190. Tras el aviso de fuerza mayor: cobertura legal más que una cancelación, pero cada retraso amenaza el reconocimiento de ingresos y frena la conversión del RPO, y el giro de OpenAI hacia arrendamientos bilaterales de capacidad añade incertidumbre de financiamiento a la estructura de Stargate; postura de esperar y ver.","source":{"basis":"streetaccount","title":"FactSet StreetAccount, Street Takeaways: Oracle Q1 Earnings, 11 September 2026, and Street Takeaways: Oracle sends force majeure notice on Project Jupiter, 24 September 2026"}},{"id":"mizuho","house":"Mizuho Securities","analysts":"Siti Panigrahi","date":"2026-10-08","rating":"Outperform","rating_class":"buy","target_usd":320,"price_at_report":144.77,"basis_short_en":"Not reported","basis_short_es":"No reportado","note_en":"Added to Mizuho's Top Picks list as the analyst's No. 1 pick (Oct 8): US$638 bn of RPO at fiscal 4Q26 on AI cloud demand; Mizuho forecasts 35% annual revenue growth from FY2026 to FY2030, to US$226 bn; risks named: outside financing for the spending and the lower gross margin of the AI cloud. The US$320 target was 25% above the Bloomberg consensus; Outperform and the target date from the Sep 9 pre-results note.","note_es":"Incorporada a la lista Top Picks de Mizuho como la selección número 1 del analista (8 oct): US$638 mil M de RPO al 4T26 fiscal por la demanda de nube de IA; Mizuho pronostica 35% de crecimiento anual de ingresos del AF2026 al AF2030, hasta US$226 mil M; riesgos señalados: financiamiento externo para el gasto y el menor margen bruto de la nube de IA. El objetivo de US$320 estaba 25% por encima del consenso de Bloomberg; Outperform y el objetivo datan de la nota previa a resultados del 9 sep.","source":{"basis":"press","title":"Oracle and these 6 stocks are newest addition to Mizuho Top Picks list, StreetInsider (Investing.com), 8 October 2026","url":"https://www.streetinsider.com/General+News/Oracle+and+these+6+stocks+are+newest+addition+to+Mizuho+Top+Picks+list/27163744.html"}},{"id":"yorkville-ives","house":"Yorkville Ives","analysts":"Dan Ives","date":"2026-10-07","rating":"In Line","rating_class":"hold","target_usd":155,"price_at_report":143.41,"basis_short_en":"Not reported","basis_short_es":"No reportado","note_en":"Initiation at In Line (Oct 7): the firm is 'staying on the sidelines until the company shows it can execute a build of this scale'; Oracle 'has built a position in AI infrastructure and retains a differentiated ability to monetize demand' but is 'funding the build at a rising cost of capital'.","note_es":"Inicio de cobertura en In Line (7 oct): la firma 'se mantiene al margen hasta que la empresa demuestre que puede ejecutar una construcción de esta escala'; Oracle 'ha construido una posición en infraestructura de IA y conserva una capacidad diferenciada para monetizar la demanda' pero 'financia la construcción a un costo de capital creciente' (traducción de FNAM).","source":{"basis":"press","title":"Yorkville Ives initiates Oracle stock coverage at In Line on execution risk, Investing.com, 7 October 2026","url":"https://www.investing.com/news/analyst-ratings/yorkville-ives-initiates-oracle-stock-coverage-at-in-line-on-execution-risk-93CH-4937090"}}],"consensusHistory":{"source":"FactSet Estimates through the FactSet AI-Ready Data connector: consensus price target (PRICE_TGT, weekly) and rating counts (weekly); a dated snapshot, the current values come from the daily FactSet file","fetched":"2026-10-05","points":[{"date":"2026-07-03","mean":254.84,"median":243,"high":400,"low":155,"count":38,"up":18,"down":5,"buy":31,"overweight":7,"hold":6,"underweight":0,"sell":1,"total":45},{"date":"2026-07-10","mean":254.84,"median":243,"high":400,"low":155,"count":38,"up":18,"down":4,"buy":31,"overweight":7,"hold":6,"underweight":0,"sell":1,"total":45},{"date":"2026-07-17","mean":252.03,"median":241,"high":400,"low":145,"count":39,"up":18,"down":4,"buy":31,"overweight":7,"hold":7,"underweight":0,"sell":1,"total":46},{"date":"2026-07-24","mean":250.87,"median":241,"high":400,"low":110,"count":39,"up":18,"down":5,"buy":31,"overweight":7,"hold":7,"underweight":0,"sell":1,"total":46},{"date":"2026-07-31","mean":250.87,"median":241,"high":400,"low":110,"count":39,"up":18,"down":5,"buy":31,"overweight":7,"hold":7,"underweight":0,"sell":1,"total":46},{"date":"2026-08-07","mean":249.85,"median":241,"high":400,"low":110,"count":39,"up":17,"down":5,"buy":30,"overweight":7,"hold":8,"underweight":0,"sell":1,"total":46},{"date":"2026-08-14","mean":249.45,"median":240.5,"high":400,"low":110,"count":38,"up":17,"down":6,"buy":29,"overweight":7,"hold":8,"underweight":0,"sell":1,"total":45},{"date":"2026-08-21","mean":249.45,"median":240.5,"high":400,"low":110,"count":38,"up":11,"down":6,"buy":29,"overweight":7,"hold":8,"underweight":0,"sell":1,"total":45},{"date":"2026-08-28","mean":249.45,"median":240.5,"high":400,"low":110,"count":38,"up":1,"down":3,"buy":29,"overweight":7,"hold":8,"underweight":0,"sell":1,"total":45},{"date":"2026-09-04","mean":246.47,"median":240,"high":400,"low":110,"count":38,"up":2,"down":6,"buy":29,"overweight":7,"hold":8,"underweight":0,"sell":1,"total":45},{"date":"2026-09-11","mean":243.87,"median":240,"high":400,"low":110,"count":38,"up":3,"down":10,"buy":30,"overweight":6,"hold":8,"underweight":0,"sell":1,"total":45},{"date":"2026-09-18","mean":242.76,"median":240,"high":400,"low":110,"count":38,"up":3,"down":12,"buy":31,"overweight":6,"hold":8,"underweight":0,"sell":1,"total":46},{"date":"2026-09-25","mean":242.84,"median":240,"high":400,"low":110,"count":37,"up":3,"down":12,"buy":30,"overweight":6,"hold":8,"underweight":0,"sell":1,"total":45},{"date":"2026-10-02","mean":242.84,"median":240,"high":400,"low":110,"count":37,"up":3,"down":12,"buy":30,"overweight":6,"hold":8,"underweight":0,"sell":1,"total":45}]}};
